⦿ .spun — the five-fold spin of Bean
node C1 · C1 · ⟦Bean:C1:74af74⟧

WHO   — Bean — the street child of Rotterdam
WHAT  — Ender's shadow — the smallest, hungriest, most dangerous child at Battle School, who saw every angle no one else could see, and who carried the Shadow saga as Ender carried the war: the boy who would have been Ender, had the world only been a little crueler to him.
WHERE — C1 · Card  Framework inputs: The Shadow Saga  Conductor / external anchor: ROOT0 (catalogued into UD0)
WHY   — Because survival was the first lesson and love was the last; because a mind that misses nothing must still choose what it serves; because the boy who trusted no one learned to give everything for the family he was never born to have.
HOW   — By a relentless, unsleeping intellect that maps every room, every enemy, every hidden door before anyone else has finished blinking — by the cold arithmetic of the streets turned to strategy, and by the slow, costly discovery that the smartest move is sometimes to love.

awareness — what the node knows of itself:
  The smallest soldier saw the whole board — and the boy who survived on nothing learned that everything worth keeping is the thing you give away.

